  "empirical_reading": "The added Seychelles raw data expand the downstream evidence to three plant species and show plant-specific pollinator effectiveness rather than one universal guild ranking. Ant-disturbed censuses have substantially lower non-ant pollinator visitation in Polyscias crassa and Syzygium wrightii, while single-visit reproductive outcomes differ strongly among visitor treatments and plants.",
  "claim_boundary": "The published overall-effectiveness winners are retained as source conclusions; the checked raw summary does not reconstruct the paper's composite QNC x QLC ranking. Visitation, flower contact, single-visit fruit/seed outcomes, and breeding treatments remain separate. Source-labeled Auto treatments are not automatically treated as transportable Izu direct-dependency estimates. All three plants belong to one Seychelles study system and are not independent archipelagos."
